.TH GAME-SUPER-RUNTIME 1 "October 2026" "0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
game-super-runtime \- configurable Linux game launch orchestration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B game-super-runtime
.RI [ --config-dir " DIR] APP-ID [OPTIONS] [--] [COMMAND ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Launch a native or Steam game using APP-ID.yaml. A supplied command takes
precedence over the profile's command. Steam launch options normally contain
.B game-super-runtime APP-ID %command%.
Missing profiles are copied from defaults.yaml or created with empty settings.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --edit
Create/open the profile in VISUAL, EDITOR or the default text editor.
.TP
.B --edit-gui
Open the local browser configuration editor.
.TP
.B --no-open
Print the GUI URL without opening a browser.
.TP
.B --validate
Validate configuration without running commands.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print a JSON launch plan. This may expose configured private environment values.
.TP
.B --doctor
Validate the plan and check host executables.
.TP
.B --config-path
Print the profile path.
.TP
.B --logs
Print the app's log directory.
.TP
.B --list
List configured app IDs (global option).
.TP
.B --edit-defaults, --edit-defaults-gui
Edit the creation template for future profiles (global options).
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/game-super-runtime/APP-ID.yaml
and
.I ~/.config/game-super-runtime/defaults.yaml
hold configuration. XDG_CONFIG_HOME, GSR_CONFIG_DIR and --config-dir override
the directory. Logs use XDG_STATE_HOME, falling back to ~/.local/state.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Child exit status is preserved. Launcher failures use 125, hook timeouts 124,
and interruptions 128 plus the signal number.
.SH NOTES
Commands are argv arrays, not shell strings. Bash scripts are explicit trusted
user code. Companion commands must stay in the foreground for group cleanup.
Proton prefixes are compatdata directories containing pfx.
.PP
Virtual directories optionally use bubblewrap and fuse-overlayfs to share folders
and merge mod layers. Targets must exist; original target files remain on disk.
See docs/virtual-directories.md for setup, manifests and persistence.
.SH SEE ALSO
.I /usr/share/doc/game-super-runtime/docs/reference.md
